    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d25">

                <pb facs="0257" n="106" xml:id="pg106"/>

                <head>25. Memorandum from President Kennedy to Bundy, August 7<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d25-f1"/></head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1961-08-07">August 7, 1961</date>
                </dateline>
                <pb facs="d25-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d25-1"/>
                <p>Seaborg recommends that we lift our laboratory experiments to one ton in his
                    letter of August 4th. It seems to me that we should consider that.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J.K.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d25-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d25-f1-content">
                <p>Presidential approval on lifting laboratory experiments to one ton. Secret. 1 p.
                    Kennedy Library, National Security Files, Subjects Series, Nuclear Testing,
                    7/16/61–8/9/61.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
